{"ts":"2026-06-10T20:00:10.707Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rj3w"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Telemetry worker: no Postgres reconnect — ingestion stalls with events stuck in RabbitMQ after postgres restart"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Incident 2026-06-09/10: pm-telemetry-postgres restarted; pm-telemetry-worker kept its dead connection and failed every insert with 'worker_insert_failed: the connection is closed' for ~24h. 15,778 events backed up in pm.telemetry.events (RabbitMQ retained all — no data loss); Postgres ingested only 11 events/24h. Manual 'docker restart pm-telemetry-worker' reconnected and drained the full backlog in ~2 min (24h count restored to 15,731). Fix needed in the worker (remote stack, scripts/prod/telemetry host): (1) reconnect/retry on closed Postgres connection instead of failing forever, (2) container healthcheck that fails on repeated insert errors so docker restarts it automatically, (3) optional: stack-health script should WARN when queue depth high while 24h ingest count is near zero."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:telemetry","infra","reliability"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-06-10T20:00:10.707Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-06-10T20:00:10.707Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5oj5"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"7a51da25a5ddb8d16825952c8ba415d0e98f8adaddaebd51d37d0878fbff0317","message":""}
