{"ts":"2026-07-04T19:18:11.320Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Context\nIncident 2026-06-09/10 on the remote telemetry stack: pm-telemetry-postgres restarted; pm-telemetry-worker kept the dead connection and failed every insert ('worker_insert_failed: the connection is closed') for ~24h. RabbitMQ retained all 15,778 backed-up events (no data loss); manual `docker restart pm-telemetry-worker` drained the backlog in ~2 min.\n\n## Fix (remote stack, scripts/prod/telemetry on the host — NOT in this repo's tracked files)\n1. Worker reconnect/retry with backoff on closed Postgres connection instead of failing forever.\n2. Container healthcheck failing on repeated insert errors so docker auto-restarts.\n3. Optional alert when queue depth grows abnormally (Grafana panel already exists).\nStanding rule: never write host IPs/tokens into tracked files; verify via scripts/prod/telemetry/check-stack-health.sh.\n\n## Definition of done\nKill-postgres drill: worker reconnects unaided and drains the queue; healthcheck restarts a wedged worker; drill evidence recorded here (counts before/after)."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-04T19:18:11.320Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"135cf73150ae06f4d1c641cde5ce408dbd337b2261556e81fe306d77dde46f9c","after_hash":"ffb28b2d183f75f8c88fbe1500ed6e2de72aa1722c9eac7ff4bfd80c0665b9cc"}
{"ts":"2026-07-12T06:14:58.725Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-12T06:14:58.724Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Second live occurrence 2026-07-12: pm-telemetry-postgres restarted ~04:00 (host maintenance window; container Up 8h vs worker Up 8d), worker logged continuous worker_insert_failed:the connection is closed, pm.telemetry.events backlogged to 111,382 messages / 1 consumer while Postgres kept serving reads. Remediation applied: docker compose restart telemetry-worker → consumer reattached, queue draining. This defect now has a repeatable operational cost on every Postgres restart — reconnect-with-backoff in the worker insert path remains the fix; consider raising priority."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-12T06:14:58.725Z"}],"before_hash":"ffb28b2d183f75f8c88fbe1500ed6e2de72aa1722c9eac7ff4bfd80c0665b9cc","after_hash":"d5ae8a73607c0c6523f2a282849ddd4eb6b03e4e41049cf6f19cd4cbe49a112b"}
